</think>The sequence  

\[
3,\; 3\sqrt{3},\; 9,\; 9\sqrt{3},\;\dots
\]

is a geometric sequence with the first term \(a_1 = 3\) and common ratio \(r = \sqrt{3}\).

For a geometric sequence, the \(n\)-th term is  

\[
a_n = a_1 \, r^{\,n-1}.
\]

Thus the recursive formula for the \(n\)-th term is obtained by setting \(n\) to be the index of the term we want to express in terms of \(n-1\):

\[
a_{n+1}=r\,a_n .
\]

Substituting \(r = \sqrt{3}\),

\[
\boxed{\,a_{n+1}= \sqrt{3}\,a_n\,}.
\]

