</think>To differentiate \(y = 2^{\sin x}\) we use the fact that \(2^{\sin x}\) can be written as \(e^{\ln 2^{\sin x}} = e^{\sin x\ln 2}\).  

Differentiate using the chain rule:

\[
\frac{dy}{dx}=e^{\sin x\ln 2}\cdot\frac{d}{dx}\bigl(\sin x\bigr)
   = e^{\sin x\ln 2}\cdot\cos x
   = 2^{\sin x}\cos x .
\]

Thus,

\[
\boxed{\,2^{\sin x}\ln 2\cos x\,}
\]

